>1) How do I proceed down from the castle level?

Behind the throne in the throne room is a secret door.  The passageway
behind this is littered with trapdoors.  These are the only way to go
down from the castle level.  Be careful before leaping into one,
though, as you will have to come back either through that passageway
or across the moat and you'll probably need to be able to levitate.

>2) My friend without net access is very unhappy with me, because he got
>his first wish for his neutral priest, and I suggested Excaliber. He
>wished for it, got it, but got somewarning message, and when he tried to
>wield it, he died! Oops....so what happened? I know only lawful characters
>can do the fountain trick with a longsword, but are non-lawful characters
>now forbidden to wield lawful artifacts?

Yep.  You're forbidden from wielding any artifact with an alignment
other than your own.  Actually, it's not impossible, but it does a
hellacious amount of damage whenever you try.  The same goes for
class-specific artifacts.

>3) He had already tried to wish for Mjollnir, and got a message that "That
>does not exist in this dungeon." What does that mean? I think his wording
>was right on the wish.

You have to be careful to phrase and spell it just so, otherwise it
will choke like that.  Try wishing for a 'blessed rustproof +2
Mjollnir.'  (I'm not sure if 'rustproof' should precede '+2' or not.
Go into Debug mode and try it both ways.)

